## 6. Canada User Conversion Flow（加拿大用户转化流程）

### 6.1 从内容到 Lead（线索）

```text
Content（教育/风险内容）
  ↓
Comment（公开问题；风险检查）
  ↓
DM（仅桥接；不收医疗资料）
  ↓
Landing Page（固定清单 CTA + 数据边界）
  ↓
Qualification（只用非临床字段）
  ↓
Human Review（人工复核）
  ↓
Next Action：checklist only / readiness call / provider referral / stop
```

| 阶段 | 自动/人工动作 | 允许记录 | Gate（闸门） | 停止条件 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Content | 草稿经事实/专业/渠道人工审核后才可授权发布 | content_id、source_ids、市场、Hook、CTA、窗口 | `approved_for_authorized_test` | 无来源、医疗承诺、未授权发布 |
| Comment | 风险路由优先；只回答公开非临床问题 | 聚合问题标签，不存用户原文到 Git | `safe_non_clinical` | 急症、诊断、病历、保证请求 |
| DM | 发送固定边界 + 安全落地页；不展开病例 | consent state、匿名 interaction_id | `consent_to_continue` | 对方发敏感资料或拒绝边界 |
| Landing Page | 领取清单、选择信息需求、申请人工沟通 | 国家、自选语言、旅行窗口、需求类别、同意 | `minimum_safe_fields` | 自由文本诱导健康披露、无隐私说明 |
| Qualification | 人工检查市场、时间、成都开放度和边界接受 | anonymous_lead_id、资格标签、阻力、下一步 | `non_clinical_qualified` | 需要医学适格、急症、未成年人 |
| Human Review | 决定清单/准备咨询/专业转介/停止 | review status、理由、风险计数 | `named_reviewer` | 无责任人、供给承诺需求 |
| Next Action | 只进入获授权的下一步 | aggregate outcome | 用户/专业/供给权限 | 报价、医院名额、病例接收未解锁 |

### 6.2 Landing Page 最小字段

允许字段：

- `country_of_residence`：只允许 Canada / other；
- `preferred_language`：English / French / Chinese / other；
- `china_familiarity`：travelled / lived / family-network / none / prefer-not-to-say；
- `planning_window`：0–3 / 3–6 / 6–12 months / exploring only；
- `information_need`：process / evidence / language / total-cost framework / aftercare / other-non-clinical；
- `chengdu_openness`：open / unsure / not currently；
- `contact_consent` 与 approved contact reference（真实联系方式不进入 Git）；
- `acknowledgement`：不提交病历、诊断、证件或支付信息。

禁止字段：诊断、症状、病史、用药、检查、影像、医生姓名、证件、生日、详细地址、银行卡、保险号和任何自由病情描述。

### 6.3 英文话术｜仅为授权后人工使用的草稿

#### 第一次评论回复

> Thanks for the question. We can share general, non-clinical information about how to evaluate a possible care-related trip to Chengdu, including roles, evidence, language, travel planning, and follow-up questions. We can’t assess medical suitability or recommend treatment here. Please don’t post medical records or personal health details. The readiness checklist is here: [approved link].

#### 第一次私信

> Thanks for reaching out. Before we continue: this is a non-clinical planning conversation, not medical advice or a hospital referral. Please do not send diagnoses, test results, images, prescriptions, ID documents, or payment information in this chat. If you only want the 10-point Chengdu care-travel readiness checklist, you can use this approved page: [approved link]. If you request a human planning call, we’ll first confirm the information boundary and consent.

#### 用户问价格

> We don’t have a verified total price to quote. A responsible estimate would need a provider-confirmed scope and validity date, plus separate medical-provider, travel, and coordination costs. We won’t publish a savings claim or fixed package price without that evidence. I can share the cost-verification checklist so you can see what a real comparison would require.

#### 用户问医院

> We can’t recommend or guarantee a Chengdu hospital at this stage. Public information about an international service is only a lead—it is not proof of a provider agreement, availability, pricing, language support, or suitability for an individual. Those items would need written provider confirmation and professional review before any formal pathway.

#### 用户问安全

> We can’t guarantee that medical travel—or Chengdu—is safe or suitable for an individual. A responsible decision would require a qualified provider’s assessment, verified emergency and transfer arrangements, aftercare planning, travel advice, and clear responsibility boundaries. If this is urgent, please use local emergency or qualified medical services in Canada rather than social media.

#### 用户问“为什么成都”

> Chengdu is being researched as a candidate destination, not presented as a proven or superior option. The current reasons to keep researching are public international-service leads, the possibility of non-clinical language and journey coordination, and the city’s travel experience. None of those proves medical quality, availability, or fit. Our first step is to learn what evidence a Canadian resident would need before Chengdu even enters their consideration set.

#### 用户说“我再考虑一下”

> Absolutely. There’s no need to make a decision now. The checklist is designed to help you identify the evidence, costs, responsibilities, and follow-up questions you would need before considering any medical trip. We won’t follow up unless you explicitly choose to hear from us.

#### 高意向用户

> Based on what you’ve shared—without any medical details—you appear interested in a non-clinical planning conversation about the evidence and logistics required to evaluate Chengdu. The next step would be a human-reviewed readiness call. It will not assess diagnosis, treatment, medical suitability, or guarantee a provider or price. Please confirm that boundary and your consent before we send the approved booking link.

#### 低意向用户

> It sounds like you’re still exploring. The best next step is the general checklist rather than a call. You can review it without sharing personal or medical information, and you can opt in later if you want a non-clinical planning conversation.

### 6.4 线索判定

| 状态 | 必须同时满足 | 不代表 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lead | 主动提交、居住加拿大、同意边界、没有敏感内容 | 真实需求或支付 |
| Qualified Lead | Canada + 3–12 月现实窗口/明确探索计划 + 对成都 open/unsure + 接受非临床边界 + 有具体信息需求 | 医学适格、医院接受、价格接受 |
